    "file": "libredwg/src/dwg.spec",
    "description": "Null pointer dereference during JSON export of a DIMENSION_RADIUS entity. The generated dwg_json_DIMENSION_RADIUS code (from dwg.spec) uses COMMON_ENTITY_DIMENSION fields without validating that required nested pointers are present for this malformed object, leading to a read at address 0x28 (zero-page offset) in dwg_json_DIMENSION_RADIUS. Crash is observed while called via dwg_json_object in out_json.c.",
    "conditions": "In llvmfuzz, attacker-controlled input is parsed into a DWG object, then randomly routed to dwg_write_json. With this PoV, parsing succeeds enough to create a malformed DIMENSION_RADIUS entity with missing/NULL internal dimension data expected by JSON serialization. When json_objects_write -> dwg_json_object dispatches to dwg_json_DIMENSION_RADIUS, the serializer dereferences the missing sub-structure and crashes. Trigger requires hitting JSON output path (case 3 in llvmfuzz switch) and a crafted DWG containing such corrupted DIMENSION_RADIUS state."
  },
